    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Latvia was proclaimed in Riga on 18 November 1918 and won its independence in a war against several enemies.</li><li>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> occupied and annexed it in 1940, and Nazi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> occupied it from 1941 to 1944.</li><li>Independence was restored in 1990–1991; Latvia joined the EU and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nato">NATO</a> in 2004 and the eurozone in 2014.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/minox">Minox</a>, a famous miniature spy camera, was first made in 1938 at the state-owned VEF electrical works in Riga.</p></aside>
    </section>

